Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:51:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 160/175] fix: the sprite bokeh report called its cutoff "stops
 over mid grey", which it is not

The budget's cutoff is a value on the cell's EXCESS over the highlight
threshold - the same weight the controller ranks by - not an absolute
luminance, so dividing it by mid grey printed a perfectly healthy frame as
"cutoff 0.001773 = -6.7 stops over mid grey": below grey, under a threshold
that is itself +2 stops above it.

The line now names the quantity, and a new "in picture terms:" line does the
translation that was wanted: the threshold, the brightness a cell needs to
keep a shape (threshold + cutoff) and the brightness at which its shape is
full (threshold + 2 x cutoff), each in stops over the mid grey in force. The
SOURCES line stopped claiming "raw above the highlight threshold" as well -
it counts the cells the splat would actually draw, i.e. past the sprite's own
sub-pixel and fade culls too. SpriteBokehSpec.md and ConsoleReference.md
carried the same mislabel and are corrected.

Report text only; no pass, no shader and no picture changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ADgAiBYv9AxSd54s1FPREm
